<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Paterson (banker)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1658–1719</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Paterson was a Scottish trader and banker, a founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-england">Bank of England</a> in 1694. He promoted the Company of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>'s Darien scheme to found a colony on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-panama">Isthmus of Panama</a> linking the Atlantic and Pacific trades; he sailed with the expedition in 1698 and survived its disastrous collapse.</p></div>
